    "body": "I don't think it's beneficial to handle this until CuPy supports arrays of `object`s.\r\n```\r\n>>> numpy.array(None)\r\narray(None, dtype=object)\r\n>>> cupy.array(None)\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"<stdin>\", line 1, in <module>\r\n  File \"/home/kataoka/cupy/cupy/creation/from_data.py\", line 45, in array\r\n    return core.array(obj, dtype, copy, order, subok, ndmin)\r\n  File \"cupy/core/core.pyx\", line 1666, in cupy.core.core.array\r\n  File \"cupy/core/core.pyx\", line 1701, in cupy.core.core.array\r\nValueError: Unsupported dtype object\r\n```",
